From dc6069256a92f1c81b617197f53db3e31a74895c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: f <f@f>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:35:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: SM8450: admit the sessions the firmware serves

The core limit of the first iris batch is the vendor's MAX_MBPF,
276480 macroblocks a frame: eight sessions of 4K.

Read on the phone on 2026-11-26 (diting, vpu20_4v, VA-API through
libva-v4l2-stateful): four sessions of 4K decode to their end, started
together and paced at 30 frames a second. Above that figure, four of 4K
with one of 1080p passed once, while three of 4K with five of 1080p,
two with nine and one with thirteen, which take the same 138720
macroblocks, ended in the firmware's fatal system error (0x5000003).
The fifth session of 4K and more ended in that error in all nine runs,
paced or not, started in the same instant or 0.5 and 2 seconds apart,
with an intra-only stream and with a stream of P-frames. So the limit
is what passed: 130560 macroblocks a frame, four sessions of 4K, which
still admits one of 8K. With it in place the fifth decoder of 4K is
refused (current session not supported(-12)), falls back to software
in ffmpeg, and the four others decode to their end.

Left as it is: thirteen and fourteen sessions of 1080p decode to
their end, and so do sixteen started a second apart; sixteen started
together end in the same error (twice of twice), fifteen ended in it in
three runs, and seventeen started half a second apart ended in it in
two of four. A limit on the frame size cannot tell these apart.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_vpu2.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_vpu2.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_vpu2.c
index e0708d618f..a6afd87c7a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_vpu2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_vpu2.c
@@ -186,6 +186,6 @@ const struct iris_platform_data sm8450_data = {
 	.requires_secure_arp = true,
 	.enc_drain_no_success = true,
 	.max_session_count = 16,
-	.max_core_mbpf = ((8192 * 4320) / 256) * 2,
+	.max_core_mbpf = ((3840 * 2176) / 256) * 4,
 	.max_core_mbps = ((3840 * 2176) / 256) * 240,
 };
